# Credentials for the kalpion-db container.
#
# Copy to `.env` beside docker-compose.yml on the VPS (/opt/ifqm-kalpion/.env).
# Docker Compose reads that file automatically; it is gitignored, and these
# values must never be committed.
#
# MARIADB_PASSWORD has to match MASTER_DB_PASS and APP_DB_PASS in
# backend/.env, or the API cannot log in to its own database.
#
# ON A DEPLOYMENT THAT IS ALREADY RUNNING, put the values it is using NOW here.
# MariaDB reads these only when it first initialises an empty data volume, so a
# different value does not change the password - it just stops matching the one
# already inside the volume, and the API can no longer sign in.
#
# Rotating properly, once this file exists and the values match:
#   docker exec -i kalpion-db mariadb -uroot -p"$MARIADB_ROOT_PASSWORD" \
#     -e "ALTER USER 'ifqm_app'@'%' IDENTIFIED BY '<new>'; FLUSH PRIVILEGES;"
# then update MARIADB_PASSWORD here and MASTER_DB_PASS / APP_DB_PASS in
# backend/.env, and redeploy. Worth doing: the previous pair was committed to a
# public repository and is in its history for good.
#
# For a NEW install, generate each one fresh:
#   openssl rand -hex 24
MARIADB_ROOT_PASSWORD=
MARIADB_PASSWORD=
